@page "/privacy"

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy - qrbound</PageTitle>

<article class="container legal-page">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-muted">Last updated: @LegalInfo.LastUpdated</p>

    <p>
        This policy explains what information qrbound ("we", "us") collects when you use qrbound.com and the
        qrbound app, how we use it, and the choices you have.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <ul>
        <li><strong>Account details</strong>: your name, email address, and, if you choose to give them, your company and mobile phone number.</li>
        <li><strong>Profile details</strong>: the information you add to your business card, such as your bio, skills, pricing and profile picture. You choose which of these appear on your card.</li>
        <li><strong>Sign-in data</strong>: passkeys (we store only the public key; your fingerprint, face or screen lock never leaves your device) and the devices you link.</li>
        <li><strong>Location</strong>: only while Ping Me is on, so people nearby can find you. Turning Ping Me off hides you straight away.</li>
        <li><strong>Contacts</strong>: the business cards you save after scanning them.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>How we use your information</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>To run your account, sign you in securely and show your business card to the people you share it with.</li>
        <li>To send you account and security messages by email and, if you opt in, by text message.</li>
        <li>To keep the service safe, prevent fraud and fix problems.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2 id="sms">Text messages (SMS)</h2>
    <p>
        If you tick the text message box when you create your account or in Settings, we will send account and security
        text messages, such as sign-in alerts and verification codes, to the mobile number you gave us.
        Opting in is optional and is not a condition of using qrbound. We keep a record of your consent (the
        number, the date and time, and the IP address it came from); changing your phone number withdraws it. You can also untick the box in Settings at any time.
        Message frequency varies. Message and
        data rates may apply. Reply <strong>STOP</strong> to stop receiving messages, or <strong>HELP</strong>
        for help. See the <a href="/terms#sms">SMS terms</a> for details.
    </p>
    <p>
        <strong>
            No mobile information will be shared with third parties or affiliates for marketing or promotional
            purposes. All the above categories exclude text messaging originator opt-in data and consent; this
            information will not be shared with any third parties.
        </strong>
    </p>

    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>
        We do not sell your personal information. We share it only:
    </p>
    <ul>
        <li>With the people you share your business card with, limited to the details you chose to show on it.</li>
        <li>With service providers who host and operate qrbound for us (for example hosting, email and text message delivery), only as needed to provide the service and never for their own marketing.</li>
        <li>When the law requires it, or to protect the rights and safety of our users.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <ul>
        <li>Edit your profile and choose what shows on your card at any time.</li>
        <li>Turn Ping Me off at any time.</li>
        <li>Untick the text message box in Settings, or reply STOP to any text message, to stop texts.</li>
        <li>Ask us to delete your account and data by emailing us.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Security and retention</h2>
    <p>
        We protect your data with encryption in transit and passkey sign-in. We keep your information while
        your account is open and delete it when you ask us to, except where the law requires us to keep it.
    </p>

    <h2>Children</h2>
    <p>qrbound is for business use and is not intended for children under 13.</p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>If we change this policy we will update the date above and, for important changes, tell you by email.</p>

    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p>Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:@LegalInfo.ContactEmail">@LegalInfo.ContactEmail</a>.</p>

    <p class="mt-4"><a href="/terms">Terms of Service</a> · <a href="/">Home</a></p>
</article>
